// schedule-v1: cap=64 events=512; in3=i64:1 in2=i64:0; in3=i64:0; in1=i64:7; in0=i64:1; in0=i64:0 in3=i64:1
{
// x-engine-firing-02: an outer arm's wake republishes `v` WAKE-tagged
// (its constant fires, `a` is stale); in the same cycle the inner select
// re-selects the arm that slept through v's REAL fire (in1=7 at e3).
// TrackedFires::deliver (wake.rs:146) sees v delivered "live" and spends
// the real bit without upgrading the tag, so the `<-` target t treats the
// value as the wake's own and keeps its last write 99.
// `graphix-fuzz run`: last epoch is [0:i64:99] (both engines).
// The same schedule without the outer sleep (e4 `in0=i64:0`, e5 `in3=i64:1`)
// ends [0:i64:7]: the event is caught up only when no outer wake coincides.
let f = |c, a, d, e| select c {
  i64:0 => {
    let v = a * i64:1;
    select d {
      i64:0 => i64:-5,
      _ => {
        let t = v + i64:0;
        t <- e ~ i64:99;
        t
      }
    }
  },
  _ => i64:-1
};
f(in0, in1, in3, in2)
}
